d is used for finish/style floor only, not for morphology."], "findings": [{"observation": "Long, thin, near-vertical strands hang from arching laterals across the whole render crown, from upper crown down to roughly mid-trunk, dominating the outer silhouette as in reference-0.", "evidence_ids": ["render-0", "reference-0"], "impact": "supported", "uncertain": false, "causal_hypothesis": null}, {"observation": "Sky is visible through large parts of the render crown interior and between strands; foliage is carried as small discrete clusters along drooping shoots rather than a solid mass.", "evidence_ids": ["render-0", "reference-0"], "impact": "supported", "uncertain": false, "causal_hypothesis": null}, {"observation": "Render trunk and larger ascending limbs are distinctly pale over their mid and upper sections, with a darker, coarser, blotchy-edged butt over roughly the lowest fifth of visible trunk.", "evidence_ids": ["render-0", "reference-0"], "impact": "supported", "uncertain": false, "causal_hypothesis": null}, {"observation": "A single stem rises from the ground in render-0 with no basal fork into co-dominant stems; the first major division occurs well above the base.", "evidence_ids": ["render-0", "reference-0"], "impact": "supported", "uncertain": false, "causal_hypothesis": null}, {"observation": "Render primaries leave the stem at moderately steep ascending angles then arch over and weep in their outer thirds, repeated at several heights.", "evidence_ids": ["render-0", "reference-0"], "impact": "supported", "uncertain": false, "causal_hypothesis": null}, {"observation": "Render stem lean is shallow and sinuous compared with reference-0's pronounced lean to viewer's left through lower and middle stem.", "evidence_ids": ["render-0", "reference-0"], "impact": "variation", "uncertain": false, "causal_hypothesis": "Individual stem posture in the reference may reflect site-specific phototropism or wind loading; no mechanism is required or asserted for the render